input.prompt:
You are building UI components for a Canvas dashboard app at `/Users/jean-patricksmith/digital/leviathan/tools/canvas/`.

Claim task #3 from the task list, then create these files.

First: `mkdir -p /Users/jean-patricksmith/digital/leviathan/tools/canvas/src/components`

Use these Tailwind patterns from the AgentPing design system:
- Card: `rounded-xl border backdrop-blur-md p-4`
- Panel: `bg-gray-900/50 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl border border-gray-800 p-4`
- Agent text: `font-mono text-sm text-cyan-400`
- Primary button: `bg-cyan-500 hover:bg-cyan-400 text-black font-medium`
- Use CSS variables from tokens.css: --bg-primary (#050505), --bg-secondary (#0a0a0a), --primary (#00e5ff), --success (#00ff9d), --warning (#ffb800), --danger (#ff2a6d)

All components receive an `onRespond: (data: Record<string, unknown>) => void` callback.

---

## 1. `src/components/CanvasRenderer.tsx` (~50 lines)

Dispatcher component:

```tsx
import { KanbanBoard } from './KanbanBoard'
import { TodoList } from './TodoList'
import { MarkdownCard } from './MarkdownCard'

interface CanvasRendererProps {
  componentType?: string;
  props?: Record<string, unknown>;
  onRespond: (data: Record<string, unknown>) => void;
}

// Map componentType to component. Unknown types show a fallback with the raw JSON.
// 'kanban' -> KanbanBoard
// 'todolist' -> TodoList  
// 'markdown' -> MarkdownCard
// default -> gray card showing "Unknown component: {type}" with JSON.stringify(props)
```

## 2. `src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx` (~200 lines)

The PRIMARY view. This is a Kanban board for BD epics/tasks.

Props shape:
```typescript
interface KanbanProps {
  columns?: string[];        // default: ['open', 'in_progress', 'blocked', 'closed']
  cards?: KanbanCard[];
}

interface KanbanCard {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  column: string;
  priority?: 'P0' | 'P1' | 'P2' | 'P3';
  type?: string;             // 'epic' | 'task' | 'bug'
  blockedBy?: string[];
  blocks?: string[];
  description?: string;
  owner?: string;
}
```

Features:
- 4 columns rendered as flex row, each column is a vertical list
- Column headers with count badge
- Cards show: ID (mono cyan), title, priority badge (colored), type badge, blocked-by count if any
- Priority colors: P0 = red/danger, P1 = amber/warning, P2 = blue/primary, P3 = gray
- Click card to expand (show description, blocked-by list, blocks list)
- HTML5 drag and drop: dragStart sets card ID, dragOver allows drop, drop fires `onRespond({ action: 'move', cardId, fromColumn, toColumn })`
- Column background: `bg-[var(--bg-secondary)] rounded-xl p-3 min-h-[200px] flex-1`
- Card: `bg-[var(--bg-tertiary)] border border-[var(--glass-border)] rounded-lg p-3 cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing hover:border-[var(--primary)]/30 transition-colors`
- Use `useState` for expanded card ID

## 3. `src/components/TodoList.tsx` (~80 lines)

Props shape:
```typescript
interface TodoListProps {
  title?: string;
  items?: TodoItem[];
}

interface TodoItem {
  id: string;
  text: string;
  checked?: boolean;
  priority?: string;
}
```

Features:
- Checkable list with custom styled checkboxes
- Check/uncheck fires `onRespond({ action: 'toggle', itemId, checked: newState })`
- Checked items get line-through and muted text
- Checkbox uses cyan accent when checked
- Items are in a glass panel

## 4. `src/components/MarkdownCard.tsx` (~40 lines)

```tsx
import ReactMarkdown from 'react-markdown'
```

Props: `{ content?: string; title?: string }`
- Renders markdown content in a glass panel
- Title in mono cyan if provided
- Style the markdown prose: headings, code blocks, links (cyan), lists
- Read-only, no onRespond interaction needed (but still accept the prop)

## 5. `src/components/ConnectionStatus.tsx` (~30 lines)

Props: `{ connected: boolean }`

- Small indicator in top-right corner style
- Green dot (#00ff9d) + "Connected" when connected
- Red dot (#ff2a6d) + "Disconnected" with pulse animation when not
- `flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono`
- Dot: `w-2 h-2 rounded-full` with appropriate color

Mark task #3 completed when done. Return a brief manifest of files created.

